Kuwait's army said Thursday it was intercepting a missile and drone attack from Iran, as Tehran targeted US allies in the Middle East. Iran has targeted US bases in Kuwait, Jordan, the United Arab Emirates, Bahrain and Iraq's autonomous Kurdistan region after extensive US bombardment on Tuesday of sites across the Islamic republic. Follow our liveblog for the latest developments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5a0a72fa-83a8-11f1-ac3d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C28P2ZQ-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5a0a72fa-83a8-11f1-ac3d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C28P2ZQ-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">972e0ef0-a728-11f1-a021-d3eaff42a4f8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 03:08:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5a0a72fa-83a8-11f1-ac3d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C28P2ZQ-1.jpg">© AFP via Sepah News screengrab</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran, US trade threats as Tehran blames Washington for wedding strike</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-iran-us-trade-threats-wedding-strike</link><description>
Iran and the United States traded threats on Wednesday after their heaviest military exchanges in weeks. Tehran accused Washington of striking a wedding party and called the attack a war crime. President Donald Trump threatened further US strikes, while Iran’s security chief warned Washington would face a “new strategy.”
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1586076a-a6e5-11f1-9f77-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-09-02-at-5-42-07-PM.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1586076a-a6e5-11f1-9f77-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-09-02-at-5-42-07-PM.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">79169d04-a734-11f1-b48b-69393fb41b1c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 01:22:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1586076a-a6e5-11f1-9f77-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-09-02-at-5-42-07-PM.png">© 7sobh</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Minneapolis apartment shooting leaves three dead, multiple injured</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260903-minneapolis-apartment-shooting</link><description>
Two people were killed and a suspect died after a shooting at a downtown Minneapolis apartment building on Wednesday, police said. Three police officers were injured, including two who suffered gunshot wounds, and were in stable condition. One victim died at the scene and another at a hospital.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b534bd2-a72a-11f1-94be-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26245835908666.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b534bd2-a72a-11f1-94be-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26245835908666.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">762d112c-a72a-11f1-b452-e9b46e204e44</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 00:01:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b534bd2-a72a-11f1-94be-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26245835908666.jpg">© Ellen Schmidt, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine warns Russian airspace ‘not safe’ in message to UN aviation watchdog</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-un-civilian-flight-safety-russian-airspace-ukraine</link><description>
Ukraine urged the UN aviation agency to call for a full ban on flights through Russian airspace, after President Volodymyr Zelensky warned it was becoming unsafe. Kyiv plans increased retaliation against intensified Russian strikes but would target only military facilities, Zelensky said, citing growing Ukrainian drone activity over Russia.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3943762-9f52-11f1-839c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/d3bbc74c16e971757a0282ef4d645e2670b58f09.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3943762-9f52-11f1-839c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/d3bbc74c16e971757a0282ef4d645e2670b58f09.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">22d4f998-a713-11f1-b7b0-d1850c402931</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 22:46:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3943762-9f52-11f1-839c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/d3bbc74c16e971757a0282ef4d645e2670b58f09.jpg">© Tetiana DZHAFAROVA, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Technology</category><title>Palantir CEO Alex Karp says French restrictions on US software are ‘backfiring’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20260902-palantir-france-digital-sovereignty</link><description>
Palantir CEO Alex Karp said on Wednesday French restrictions limiting government use of US-made software were proving counterproductive. His comments followed France’s decision to replace Palantir with domestic provider ChapsVision at intelligence agency DGSI over data sovereignty concerns. Karp said Europe’s regulatory environment was hurting competitiveness.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0c2d0aa-a713-11f1-bd3a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/9d9db451a6a010316d34af039aa69c796b86b602.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0c2d0aa-a713-11f1-bd3a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/9d9db451a6a010316d34af039aa69c796b86b602.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e600daca-a715-11f1-a04d-c1d6529d5029</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 22:13:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0c2d0aa-a713-11f1-bd3a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/9d9db451a6a010316d34af039aa69c796b86b602.jpg">© Matt Ramey, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Culture</category><title>Venice Film Festival opens with George Clooney, Murdoch film and geopolitics</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/culture/20260902-venice-film-festival-clooney-murdoch-film-geopolitics</link><description>
George Clooney used a Venice Film Festival appearance on Wednesday to weigh in on artificial intelligence, media ownership and US politics while receiving a lifetime achievement award. Clooney warned Hollywood must adapt to AI and criticised growing billionaire control of major media platforms.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e7c5742-a6f8-11f1-89a5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/e0a235f6e6cdda43533bcbf1c133ff86b2451808.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e7c5742-a6f8-11f1-89a5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/e0a235f6e6cdda43533bcbf1c133ff86b2451808.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c744cb60-a719-11f1-9001-331dca5836da</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 22:11:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e7c5742-a6f8-11f1-89a5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/e0a235f6e6cdda43533bcbf1c133ff86b2451808.jpg">© Stefano RELLANDINI, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Malta acquits tycoon Yorgen Fenech in investigative journalist murder case</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-reporter-murder</link><description>
A Maltese court on Wednesday acquitted tycoon Yorgen Fenech of orchestrating the 2017 car-bomb killing of investigative journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia, a verdict that drew condemnation from her family and press freedom advocates. Her family said the acquittal denied Caruana Galizia justice, while her son called it a “terrible decision.”
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e575ea4-a714-11f1-96e8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-02T211806Z-686920899-RC26BNAZQ7CO-RTRMADP-3-MALTA-DAPHNE-TRIAL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e575ea4-a714-11f1-96e8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-02T211806Z-686920899-RC26BNAZQ7CO-RTRMADP-3-MALTA-DAPHNE-TRIAL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ef7a451c-a717-11f1-a7ec-c1d6529d5029</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 21:56:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e575ea4-a714-11f1-96e8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-02T211806Z-686920899-RC26BNAZQ7CO-RTRMADP-3-MALTA-DAPHNE-TRIAL.jpg">© Darrin Zammit Lupi, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Is Wintour still en vogue? Met navigates rough seas as Galliano retrospective sinks into 'Horizons'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260902-is-wintour-still-en-vogue-the-met-navigates-rough-seas-as-galliano-s-horizons-sparks-controversy</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Dana Thomas, author of Gods and Kings: The Rise and Fall of Alexander McQueen and John Galliano, and the New York Times bestseller Deluxe: How Luxury Lost Its Luster. The fiery controversy over the Met's now-cancelled John Galliano retrospective challenges the timeless debate over whether art can be separated from the artist. Our guest argues that the key issue is institutional power. From her perspective, Galliano’s stature as an artist and fashion designer is never in dispute. All the while, his character has been once again very publicly called into question.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0835833a-a715-11f1-95e0-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-19454179796a9894a34fae85-67989697.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0835833a-a715-11f1-95e0-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-19454179796a9894a34fae85-67989697.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ce7e9cb0-a716-11f1-a20c-331dca5836da</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 21:39:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Outrage as Maltese tycoon acquitted of reporter Daphne Caruana Galizia's murder</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/outrage-as-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-of-reporter-daphne-caruana-galizia-s-murder</link><description>
A Maltese court on Wednesday acquitted tycoon Yorgen Fenech of orchestrating the car-bomb killing of investigative reporter Daphne Caruana Galizia, sparking outrage from her family and media freedom advocates. The wealthy businessman had stood accused of masterminding the 2017 assassination of 53-year-old Caruana Galizia, which sparked unprecedented protests and brought down a government. MaltaToday Executive Editor Kurt Sansone speaks with FRANCE 24.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6756d88-75e3-11eb-bc3d-005056a964fe/w:1024/p:16x9/malta-51.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6756d88-75e3-11eb-bc3d-005056a964fe/w:1024/p:16x9/malta-51.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">842fcd12-a713-11f1-a180-d1850c402931</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 21:20:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>US-Iran war: Old videos falsely claim to show new attacks on American bases</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-iran-war-old-videos-falsely-claim-to-show-new-attacks-on-american-bases-1</link><description>
As US-Iran hostilities flare up and strikes has resumed, so has a wave of misinformation online. Old and unrelated videos are flooding social media, falsely presented as footage of new attacks. As tensions escalate, lips filmed in Dubai, Russia and the US have been misrepresented as Iranian strikes on US bases in the Gulf. Another 68-year-old video of a US nuclear test has been falsely claimed to show Iran detonating mines in the Strait of Hormuz. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/746a965a-a70e-11f1-9bb5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15220706936a98899a7c8783-61126554.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/746a965a-a70e-11f1-9bb5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15220706936a98899a7c8783-61126554.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3d86616e-a70e-11f1-9462-b37d75498e93</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 20:57:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US oversees signing of ‘billions’ in deals between Venezuela and Chevron, ENI, GE</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260902-us-oversees-signing-of-billions-in-deals-between-venezuela-and-chevron-eni-ge</link><description>
US oil giant Chevron, Italy's ENI and GE Vernova signed deals worth "tens of billions of dollars" with Venezuela, US Energy Secretary Chris Wright said Wednesday during a trip to Caracas where he and Interim President Delcy Rodriguez finalised the agreements. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a54a385a-a70b-11f1-84cf-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26245635811814.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a54a385a-a70b-11f1-84cf-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26245635811814.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b7ff0714-a70b-11f1-90c3-b37d75498e93</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 20:54:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a54a385a-a70b-11f1-84cf-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26245635811814.jpg">© Pedro Mattey, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Kenyan editor found safe after abduction</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/kenyan-editor-found-safe-after-abduction</link><description>
In tonight's edition, rights groups in Kenya call for an investigation after a top journalist is abducted overnight  by heavily armed men. Also, trials for three potential vaccines against the Bunjeebuyyoo strain of Ebola are due to start over the next couple of months. And Senegalese consumers who are frustrated by the rising cost of living have launched a new campaign. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/81e27734-a70a-11f1-9e93-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260902-2141-Live-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/81e27734-a70a-11f1-9e93-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260902-2141-Live-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c6b02712-a70a-11f1-a83d-b37d75498e93</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 20:15:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Chevron, Eni commit to expand oil projects in Venezuela under US eye</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/chevron-eni-commit-to-expand-oil-projects-in-venezuela-under-us-eye</link><description>
U.S.' Chevron, Italy's Eni and other foreign energy producers committed on Wednesday to major project expansions to boost oil output in Venezuela, in a signing ceremony in Caracas overseen by interim President ​Delcy Rodriguez and ‌U.S. Energy Secretary Chris Wright. FRANCE 24's Maya Yataghene reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5cdfb286-07b8-11f1-9ba1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-02-11T193438Z-319517799-RC2UJJA5DK2G-RTRMADP-3-VENEZUELA-USA-OIL-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5cdfb286-07b8-11f1-9ba1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-02-11T193438Z-319517799-RC2UJJA5DK2G-RTRMADP-3-VENEZUELA-USA-OIL-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2f36c30e-a706-11f1-8ddb-33773faa09bf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 20:00:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Zelensky warns airlines Russian skies not safe due to Ukraine drones</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/zelensky-warns-airlines-russian-skies-not-safe-due-to-ukraine-drones</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky warned Tuesday that his country's drones would make Russia's airspace "completely unsafe" for the duration of the war, drawing accusations of "state terrorism" from Russian leader Vladimir Putin. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Former British Military Intelligence Officer Philip Ingram explains that Zelensky's warning is addressed to "those international airlines from the Middle East, from South East Asia, China included that are still operating into Moscow" adding that "it's all part of the information war and bringing the overall conflict to the Russian people".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28e9c598-7e7d-11f1-9486-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-12T130639Z-1873803642-RC2LZLA3LE8L-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-DRONES-GERMANY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28e9c598-7e7d-11f1-9486-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-12T130639Z-1873803642-RC2LZLA3LE8L-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-DRONES-GERMANY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9bc3e66c-a703-11f1-b090-33773faa09bf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 19:32:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Spanish report flags Moroccan police's 'total permissiveness' in Ceuta migrant rush</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260902-spanish-report-flags-moroccan-police-s-total-permissiveness-in-ceuta-migrant-rush</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">c3d35a98-a703-11f1-b245-7df714f7ef0c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 19:23:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Spanish report flags Moroccan police's 'total permissiveness' in Ceuta migrant rush</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260902-spanish-report-flags-moroccan-police-s-total-permissiveness-in-ceuta-migrant-rush</link><description>
Moroccan security forces displayed "total permissiveness" during last month's massive wave of migrants who crossed into the Spanish North African territory of Ceuta, according to a Spanish police report seen by a French news agency on Wednesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cf6d932-a517-11f1-b815-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26233420530465.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cf6d932-a517-11f1-b815-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26233420530465.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1ffac56a-a702-11f1-a811-33773faa09bf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 19:20:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cf6d932-a517-11f1-b815-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26233420530465.jpg">© Antonio Sempere, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Live: Macron and Charles III visit historic Bayeux tapestry exhibition together</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-france-s-macron-in-britain-to-help-unveil-bayeux-tapestry</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">0492aa12-a6f9-11f1-9083-2ff77675d9fc</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 18:09:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>Israeli FM Gideon Sa'ar: 'I hope Iran will not make the mistake of attacking us'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260902-israeli-fm-gideon-sa-ar-i-hope-iran-will-not-make-the-mistake-of-attacking-us</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, Israel's Minister of Foreign Affairs Gideon Sa’ar addressed the resumption in fighting between the US and Iran, and warned that any Iranian attack on Israel would trigger a "severe" response. He also accused Tehran of continuing to pursue "nuclear weapons aspirations", claiming that Israel "will not allow" Iran to achieve them. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be03f3b8-a6e8-11f1-aab9-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/TAT-SAAR-POUR-MIX.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be03f3b8-a6e8-11f1-aab9-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/TAT-SAAR-POUR-MIX.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ed61f0d6-a6e0-11f1-b900-bbccc4313f26</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 17:49:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Videos and debris raise questions over alleged US strike on Iranian wedding</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-videos-and-debris-raise-questions-over-alleged-us-strike-on-iranian-wedding</link><description>
On the evening of September 1, a barrage of US missile and drone attacks on a town in southern Iran allegedly struck a wedding ceremony, killing at least five people, including a four-year-old boy. FRANCE 24 geolocated a direct hit to the civilian building where local residents say the wedding was being held. The building was more than 135 meters from the apparent target, a communications tower.
